@startuml sequence_qml_string_marshaling
!theme plain
title QML Shell — String Marshaling (JS ↔ C++)

participant "QtShellMgr\n(JS)" as js
participant "WASM Heap\n(Module.HEAPU8)" as heap
participant "qtshell.wasm\n(C++)" as cpp

note over js, cpp
  **Why manual marshaling?**
  Qt's qt_add_executable overrides Emscripten's
  EXPORTED_RUNTIME_METHODS, stripping ccall / cwrap /
  _malloc / _free. The C functions are still exported
  via EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE, so we call them directly
  with manual UTF-8 string encoding.
end note

== 1. Allocate: _allocUTF8(jsString) ==

js -> js : encoder = new TextEncoder()\nencoded = encoder.encode(jsString)

js -> cpp : _qtshell_malloc(encoded.length + 1)
activate cpp
cpp -> cpp : malloc(len + 1)
cpp --> js : ptr (heap offset)
deactivate cpp

js -> heap : Module.HEAPU8.set(encoded, ptr)
activate heap
heap -> heap : Copy UTF-8 bytes\nto WASM linear memory
heap --> js
deactivate heap

js -> heap : HEAPU8[ptr + len] = 0
activate heap
heap -> heap : Write null terminator
heap --> js
deactivate heap

== 2. Call: Module._qtshell_XXX(ptr) ==

js -> cpp : Module._qtshell_XXX(ptr)
activate cpp
cpp -> cpp : const char* arg = (const char*)ptr
cpp -> cpp : QString str =\n  QString::fromUtf8(arg)
note right: C++ now has a proper\nQString copy of the data
cpp -> cpp : (process the string...)
cpp --> js : (return)
deactivate cpp

== 3. Free: _qtshell_free(ptr) ==

js -> cpp : _qtshell_free(ptr)
activate cpp
cpp -> cpp : free(ptr)
note right: Release WASM heap memory
cpp --> js
deactivate cpp

== Example: _callWithString() ==

note over js, cpp
  **Helper pattern used throughout QtShellManager.js:**
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  function _callWithString(funcName, str) {
    var func = _shellModule['_' + funcName];
    var ptr = _allocUTF8(str);
    try {
      func(ptr);
    } finally {
      _shellModule._qtshell_free(ptr);
    }
  }
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Used for: qtshell_setServiceName,
            qtshell_loadQmlSource (2 ptrs),
            qtshell_onResponse (2 ptrs),
            qtshell_onError (2 ptrs)
end note

@enduml
